# smartcard — reading smart card devices on Linux

## Install the reader stack (openSUSE Tumbleweed)

```sh
sudo zypper install pcsc-lite pcsc-tools opensc pcsc-ccid
```

## Enable and start the PC/SC daemon

```sh
sudo systemctl enable --now pcscd.service
```

## Scan for a reader and watch card insert/remove events

```sh
# Live monitor — insert or remove the card to see status change
pcsc_scan
```

## Inspect the reader and the inserted card

```sh
# List readers and card details
opensc-tool -l -n

# Browse the card's filesystem interactively
opensc-explorer
```

## Load the PKCS#11 module in Firefox

```
Settings → Privacy & Security → Certificates → Security Devices…
Load → Name: OpenSC PKCS#11
Module path: /usr/lib64/opensc-pkcs11.so
```

## Tool reference

| Tool             | Purpose                                  |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| pcsc_scan        | live reader/card status monitor          |
| opensc-tool -l   | list connected readers                   |
| opensc-explorer  | browse the card's on-disk structure      |
| opensc-pkcs11.so | PKCS#11 module for browsers/apps          |

> On Tumbleweed the PKCS#11 module lives under `/usr/lib64/`, not the
> Debian-style `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/` path.
